WEBVTT

00:10.910 --> 00:12.940
Dad, what are you doing?

00:12.940 --> 00:16.230
I can't say I'm exactly sure myself.

00:16.230 --> 00:19.430
I'm supposed to fight Mr. Ashcroft.

00:25.180 --> 00:26.330
He's a nobody.

00:26.860 --> 00:28.240
What was that?

00:28.240 --> 00:30.510
I don't care if you're the Demon King slayer.

00:30.510 --> 00:33.250
Once I've beaten the Red Ogre,
 you're next, girl.

00:48.480 --> 00:56.740
<b>My Daughter Left the Nest and Returned an S-Rank Adventurer</b>

02:07.270 --> 02:12.690
<b>Episode 6 "Rebels Acting in Secret"</b>

02:10.170 --> 02:13.010
Crush him, Dad.

02:17.930 --> 02:22.000
<i>Now that we're doing this, 
it'd be rude to hold back.</i>

02:36.740 --> 02:38.590
I knew you'd beat him, Master!

02:38.590 --> 02:40.900
Well, Ash? Have you learned your place?

02:41.670 --> 02:44.020
I knew it. My dad is super strong.

02:44.020 --> 02:46.180
Actually, uh...

02:47.240 --> 02:48.970
I refuse to acknowledge this.

02:48.970 --> 02:51.780
Lady Sasha, that was an accident.

02:51.780 --> 02:54.770
His sword simply struck me 
when he slipped in the mud.

02:54.990 --> 02:57.420
Don't be a sore loser.
You disgrace yourself.

02:57.420 --> 03:02.270
You think that kind of excuse 
would work on the battlefield?

03:04.360 --> 03:10.170
By pretending to slip, 
he evaded your blow while attacking.

03:10.170 --> 03:12.990
And you're making excuses after falling for it.

03:12.990 --> 03:14.630
No, Lady Sasha.

03:15.010 --> 03:17.850
I could hardly call that a victory.

03:18.310 --> 03:20.540
Say no more, Master.

03:20.540 --> 03:22.920
You needn't be so considerate of this man.

03:22.920 --> 03:25.730
No, I'm serious...

03:26.940 --> 03:31.780
It would seem you have 
struggles of your own, Mr. Belgrieve.

03:32.930 --> 03:34.440
Nothing like yours.

03:36.720 --> 03:40.250
You said you'd fight me after my dad, right?

03:41.360 --> 03:43.700
N-No, I...

03:43.940 --> 03:45.800
No!

03:48.360 --> 03:51.670
Ange, we all know you're strong.

03:51.670 --> 03:57.550
But that doesn't mean it's okay
for you to pick a one-sided fight.

03:58.530 --> 04:01.170
But Dad, he started it.

04:01.170 --> 04:03.910
Even if the other party is to blame,

04:03.910 --> 04:07.520
is that any reason for you to get 
carried away and do as you please?

04:07.520 --> 04:08.850
Mr. Belgrieve.

04:09.380 --> 04:11.570
I am the one at fault here.

04:11.570 --> 04:14.390
Please don't scold Ms. Angeline.

04:14.660 --> 04:17.680
But she injured you.
This will affect your duties.

04:17.680 --> 04:21.520
Then I should have controlled myself.

04:21.740 --> 04:27.190
I'm truly sorry for causing unnecessary 
commotion because of my ridiculous jealousy.

04:27.750 --> 04:30.230
Besides, this isn't as bad as it looks.

04:31.680 --> 04:34.450
That's very gracious of you.

04:34.450 --> 04:37.810
Ange, apologize to Mr. Ashcroft.

04:38.590 --> 04:39.640
But...

04:39.640 --> 04:40.790
Angeline.

04:41.500 --> 04:42.840
I'm sorry.

04:43.120 --> 04:48.080
Mr. Belgrieve, I'm also to blame
for suggesting a duel.

04:48.080 --> 04:50.600
We egged him on, too.

04:50.600 --> 04:53.430
It's not just Ange's fault.

04:53.430 --> 04:55.820
Mr. Ashcroft, we apologize.

04:55.820 --> 04:57.380
Sorry.

04:57.960 --> 04:59.730
Don't mention it.

05:00.050 --> 05:02.170
You've got good friends.

05:03.110 --> 05:08.990
Now, that was something,
but I'm sure you're busy, Lady Helvetica.

05:08.990 --> 05:12.490
Pay us no mind.
You can return to your affairs.

05:12.690 --> 05:15.380
How very considerate of you.

05:15.380 --> 05:17.240
I think I'll do just that.

05:17.540 --> 05:22.760
Since Ash can't move, let's speak in here.

05:23.350 --> 05:27.000
Count Malta will be coming soon.

05:28.870 --> 05:31.340
Well, we'll see ourselves out.

05:32.520 --> 05:33.100
Come on.

05:33.100 --> 05:34.630
O-Okay.

05:35.850 --> 05:37.150
<i>Good grief.</i>

05:37.150 --> 05:39.380
<i>I don't know if she's just trusting</i>

05:39.380 --> 05:43.640
<i>or if she means to rope us in
 by making sure we overhear.</i>

05:43.640 --> 05:47.160
<i>I don't want to think she's
 that kind of person, but...</i>

05:47.900 --> 05:50.060
Welp, what should we do now?

05:50.420 --> 05:53.020
Since we're here, 
shall we go out on the town?

05:54.090 --> 05:55.520
Sounds nice.

05:56.390 --> 05:58.360
Don't be so upset.

05:58.360 --> 06:02.540
I know you were angry on my behalf.

06:03.740 --> 06:05.840
I'll forgive you if you pick me up.

06:13.070 --> 06:16.190
Perhaps I should've fawned 
on my father more.

06:16.670 --> 06:20.990
Mr. Bel, Sasha would like 
to be picked up, too!

06:20.990 --> 06:23.220
Wh-What? Ms. Miri!

06:28.870 --> 06:30.350
Hello up there!

06:30.630 --> 06:32.010
This brings back memories.

06:32.010 --> 06:36.470
My father carried me like 
this when I was young.

06:36.470 --> 06:37.870
Is that so?

06:38.110 --> 06:41.350
Mr. Bel, I'm next.

06:41.350 --> 06:43.100
Not you, Miri. You're too heavy.

06:43.100 --> 06:45.100
Hey, who are you calling fat?!

06:45.100 --> 06:46.330
I didn't say that.

06:46.330 --> 06:48.640
It's the same thing!

06:49.160 --> 06:51.670
Aw, c'mon! Jeez!

06:52.870 --> 06:53.930
Hear me.

06:53.930 --> 06:57.770
Turn especially powerful monsters 
on the Bordeaux estate.

06:57.770 --> 07:02.020
Those impudent girls must die!

07:02.370 --> 07:05.520
What a foolish man. He's mad with power.

07:05.520 --> 07:09.310
He reminds me of those clergymen
 in name only in Lucrecia.

07:09.310 --> 07:11.420
I'm going to change this world!

07:11.420 --> 07:12.770
Whatever you say.

07:14.080 --> 07:16.390
Kingdom of the outcasts...

07:16.390 --> 07:18.290
Tailwind of the wanderer...

07:18.290 --> 07:21.170
They condemn us as evil.

07:21.170 --> 07:23.920
Curtains descend on the closed gate of dusk.

07:24.340 --> 07:26.560
Oh, this arduous path to tread!

07:33.770 --> 07:34.940
This is the place.

07:35.210 --> 07:38.920
I wanted to introduce you all
 to the guild master.

07:39.270 --> 07:43.950
Welcome. Thank you for coming all this way.

07:43.950 --> 07:47.620
This is Mr. Elmore,
the man in charge of our guild.

07:47.620 --> 07:48.910
And these are—

07:48.910 --> 07:51.030
I know who they are.

07:51.030 --> 07:53.160
It's a pleasure to meet you.

07:53.160 --> 07:58.120
I run the adventurer's guild here in Bordeaux.

07:58.310 --> 08:00.900
I appreciate the warm welcome.

08:00.900 --> 08:03.110
Sorry to drop in while you're working.

08:03.110 --> 08:07.270
Oh, hardly. I didn't have 
much work to do anyway.

08:07.270 --> 08:08.950
Please, have a seat.

08:11.130 --> 08:12.830
Gosh, this room is so pretty.

08:12.830 --> 08:15.590
You're nothing like the 
guild master of Orphen.

08:15.590 --> 08:16.460
Hey, now...

08:16.780 --> 08:20.480
I'm sure Mr. Lionel is doing his best.

08:20.850 --> 08:27.470
I'm impressed how he handled the monster 
infestation that the Demon King caused.

08:27.810 --> 08:31.170
Bordeaux could've sent reinforcements,

08:31.170 --> 08:35.490
though we currently have
 no S-rank adventurers.

08:35.490 --> 08:37.270
What's your rank, Mr. Elmore?

08:37.530 --> 08:39.830
I was Double A.

08:39.830 --> 08:42.910
I lacked the talent for adventuring,

08:42.910 --> 08:46.530
but strangely, office work seems to suit me.

08:47.980 --> 08:53.170
Our guild master says it's an 
easy job for people with no talent.

08:53.550 --> 08:55.300
Hey, Ange!

08:55.300 --> 08:59.480
Yes, yes, I'm sure that's true 
of most guilds these days.

08:59.480 --> 09:03.150
But Bordeaux is a little different.

09:03.150 --> 09:07.050
Our guild has always been tied to the county.

09:07.410 --> 09:12.730
Nobles typically shun adventurers, 
but Bordeaux was originally a local family.

09:13.160 --> 09:16.250
We have an affinity for the profession.

09:16.250 --> 09:22.110
We've even established a system for the guild 
to coordinate with soldiers in emergencies.

09:22.110 --> 09:26.500
This guild contributes 
to the town's defenses.

09:26.500 --> 09:27.990
Huh.

09:28.260 --> 09:34.100
<i>I see. Still, the town guard and 
adventurers don't ordinarily get along.</i>

09:34.100 --> 09:35.500
<i>I wonder what other nobles,</i>

09:35.500 --> 09:38.660
<i>especially from the heartland,
 would think if they came here.</i>

09:41.600 --> 09:43.210
That's odd.

09:43.210 --> 09:45.390
The sky was clear until a moment ago.

09:45.390 --> 09:48.200
I feel an unpleasant prickling sensation.

09:49.110 --> 09:50.980
Guild master, it's an emergency!

09:50.980 --> 09:52.110
What is it?

09:52.350 --> 09:55.910
A large number of undead have 
risen in the graveyard!

09:59.380 --> 10:00.660
Charlotte.

10:01.060 --> 10:02.450
Charlotte.

10:05.220 --> 10:07.050
Come here, Charlotte.

10:07.050 --> 10:09.990
We love you, our darling daughter,
 more than anything.

10:10.300 --> 10:13.790
Goddess Vienna blessed us with a saint.

10:14.800 --> 10:17.280
Her white hair, her red eyes...

10:17.280 --> 10:18.240
Everything.

10:21.330 --> 10:22.720
We'll never forgive you!

10:22.720 --> 10:23.950
We'll show you!

10:24.510 --> 10:27.860
Why? We prayed each and every day.

10:27.860 --> 10:31.030
We did lots of good things for Vienna.

10:31.390 --> 10:35.090
Damn it. All the pope cares about is money.

10:35.090 --> 10:37.350
You must run, Charlotte.

10:38.020 --> 10:41.270
No! I'm staying with both of you!

10:41.570 --> 10:44.990
It's all right. We'll be right behind you.

10:46.570 --> 10:49.970
Dad... Mom!

11:05.090 --> 11:07.040
Poor girl.

11:08.150 --> 11:12.660
Reduced to begging, and persecuted 
with no one to save you.

11:13.100 --> 11:15.070
Do you hate the cult of Vienna?

11:16.260 --> 11:18.620
I do. I hate them.

11:18.620 --> 11:21.060
They took everything from me.

11:21.620 --> 11:25.080
Then I shall lend you the power of Solomon.

11:25.900 --> 11:29.830
Use this to awaken people 
from the cult of Vienna.

11:30.530 --> 11:33.400
Behold Samigina's ring.

11:36.340 --> 11:39.580
Now, I'll show them a miracle.

11:50.220 --> 11:51.140
This way!

11:51.140 --> 11:53.020
I saw the ominous clouds,

11:53.020 --> 11:55.960
then a horde of undead 
sprang up in the graveyard!

11:55.960 --> 11:57.780
<i>I knew it. Those clouds...</i>

11:58.170 --> 11:59.930
<i>Did someone summon them?</i>

12:01.560 --> 12:04.010
This isn't good. Everyone's panicking.

12:04.960 --> 12:07.170
Yeah, we can't get through.

12:07.920 --> 12:10.060
Stay calm, everyone!

12:10.060 --> 12:12.460
Follow the soldiers' instructions!

12:13.700 --> 12:15.280
Sorry to keep you waiting.

12:15.280 --> 12:17.220
Leave the evacuation effort to me.

12:43.140 --> 12:46.960
That's the S-rank party we saw yesterday!

12:56.420 --> 12:59.700
This'll be a good warm-up
 before returning to Orphen.

13:00.620 --> 13:02.990
Gotta get back into the swing of things.

13:02.990 --> 13:05.380
We'll be a laughingstock
if we're out of practice.

13:05.870 --> 13:08.630
It's been too long! Let's go wild!

13:08.630 --> 13:12.130
Wow, they really are an S-rank party!

13:12.130 --> 13:13.820
We can't let them show us up!

13:13.820 --> 13:16.310
Show them what Bordeaux's 
adventurers can do!

13:16.310 --> 13:17.640
Yeah!

13:19.150 --> 13:22.100
<i>So this is the Black-Haired Valkyrie.</i>

13:22.100 --> 13:23.810
<i>She's grown so strong.</i>

13:29.790 --> 13:32.230
No time to stand around being sentimental.

13:32.230 --> 13:33.490
Thank you.

13:33.490 --> 13:35.580
Wait, you're the Red Ogre!

13:35.580 --> 13:37.600
I'm not worth much, but I'm happy to help.

13:38.040 --> 13:39.010
Master!

13:39.450 --> 13:41.550
The people have now been evacuated.

13:41.550 --> 13:43.870
Lady Sasha and Mr. Elmore.

13:43.870 --> 13:45.750
Something terrible has happened.

13:45.750 --> 13:47.620
The barrier won't activate.

13:47.620 --> 13:49.990
Then there's no holding back the undead.

13:52.920 --> 13:55.880
The clouds are thickest 
around the Bordeaux estate.

13:55.880 --> 13:58.400
They came from the west. From Hazel.

13:59.390 --> 14:03.880
<i>That's the town where the noble
who's opposing the Bordeaux family lives.</i>

14:04.350 --> 14:07.480
Mr. Elmore, are most of the adventurers here?

14:07.480 --> 14:13.250
Yes. Aside from those guarding the citizens, 
most of the soldiers are here as well.

14:13.250 --> 14:15.900
Someone may be behind this.

14:15.900 --> 14:20.170
Yes. It's odd for something like 
this to happen with no warning.

14:20.170 --> 14:22.980
I'm heading to the Bordeaux estate.

14:22.980 --> 14:25.290
I've got a bad feeling about this.

14:25.510 --> 14:29.670
I'll go with you. Please handle things here.

14:30.620 --> 14:32.010
I appreciate it.

14:32.010 --> 14:33.840
Is the countess in trouble?

14:33.840 --> 14:35.350
We're coming, too!

14:45.450 --> 14:47.960
Defend this place with your lives!

14:47.960 --> 14:51.260
Don't let them get one step closer 
to Lady Helvetica and Lady Seren!

14:51.260 --> 14:51.920
Yes, sir!

14:53.490 --> 14:54.360
What is that?!

14:54.360 --> 14:55.650
A high-rank creature.

14:55.650 --> 14:58.860
Look alive, everyone!
That's no ordinary undead!

15:23.430 --> 15:26.150
This is what I get for not knowing my place.

15:26.460 --> 15:29.590
I can't fight at full 
strength during an emergency

15:29.590 --> 15:32.490
because of a spat 
my foolish pride got me into.

15:33.320 --> 15:34.000
However...

15:36.350 --> 15:40.910
<i>I'll pay for all I've been given
 with my life!</i>

15:43.720 --> 15:45.260
Wh-What's that?

15:47.870 --> 15:50.250
Are you all right, Mr. Ashcroft?

15:50.950 --> 15:53.620
Mr. Belgrieve! Mr. Elmore.

15:53.620 --> 15:56.940
I'm glad we made it in time. 
Where is Lady Helvetica?

15:57.600 --> 15:58.910
In the room behind me.

15:59.340 --> 16:01.470
But what are you two doing here?

16:02.320 --> 16:06.550
I kinda had a hunch, but I can't believe 
there are high-rank undead here.

16:06.550 --> 16:08.850
In any event, I'm glad you're all right.

16:10.500 --> 16:12.880
Don't let your guard down yet.

16:12.880 --> 16:14.730
We've gotta get out of here.

16:15.630 --> 16:17.170
You're right.

16:18.580 --> 16:20.790
Lady Helvetica, Lady Seren!

16:20.790 --> 16:22.370
We've thinned the enemy.

16:22.370 --> 16:23.690
We should evacuate.

16:32.470 --> 16:34.090
Where is Dad?

16:34.090 --> 16:35.620
Look, the clouds!

16:42.190 --> 16:43.660
<i>This feeling...</i>

16:47.570 --> 16:51.570
Return... home...

16:54.580 --> 16:56.230
A darkwalker.

16:56.230 --> 16:58.820
Light magic! Make light!

17:04.510 --> 17:06.680
This is our chance! Attack!

17:06.680 --> 17:08.170
Yeah!

17:08.470 --> 17:11.540
Ane and Miri, handle the horde.

17:24.130 --> 17:26.980
<i>There's no resistance. What is this?</i>

17:31.200 --> 17:32.950
That didn't hurt at all.

17:33.340 --> 17:34.650
Papier-mâché?

17:43.970 --> 17:46.740
<i>My injury from back then is hurting now?</i>

17:46.740 --> 17:49.030
It turned into mist.

17:50.440 --> 17:51.930
What is this?

17:51.930 --> 17:54.890
It's mist, but suddenly it feels heavy.

17:55.490 --> 17:57.050
You're the same.

17:57.940 --> 18:04.220
You're the same... You're the same...
You're the same... You're the same...

18:02.940 --> 18:04.220
What's going on?

18:04.220 --> 18:05.040
Ange!

18:05.040 --> 18:07.240
What is this? What's happening?

18:07.240 --> 18:16.570
Let's go home... Let's go home...
Let's go home... Let's go home...

18:12.880 --> 18:13.980
No...

18:14.750 --> 18:16.570
No!

18:18.560 --> 18:19.700
Sasha...

18:19.700 --> 18:22.120
Can you stand? Let's retreat.

18:23.150 --> 18:25.830
Sorry, Sasha. I'm useless.

18:28.570 --> 18:30.660
The S-ranker lost?

18:30.660 --> 18:35.090
How are we supposed 
to attack an enemy that strong?

18:39.160 --> 18:41.080
There's more of them?

18:41.080 --> 18:43.160
What do we do?

18:43.160 --> 18:44.350
Hey!

18:44.350 --> 18:46.410
It's dangerous! Turn back!

18:46.410 --> 18:47.980
Fret not.

18:51.350 --> 18:54.850
Behold the miracles of Solomon!

19:05.420 --> 19:08.240
The danger has passed, everyone.

19:08.240 --> 19:11.450
Wh-Who is she?

19:11.720 --> 19:13.640
My name is Charlotte.

19:13.640 --> 19:17.350
I travel the land in 
order to save the world.

19:18.800 --> 19:21.340
Well, well. If it isn't Lady Sasha.

19:21.870 --> 19:24.540
You seem to be struggling quite a bit.

19:25.180 --> 19:28.270
Count Malta, what are you doing here?

19:28.590 --> 19:32.420
I noticed some strange clouds 
rolling in from the west.

19:32.420 --> 19:35.830
According to Ms. Charlotte, 
who happened to be staying with me,

19:35.830 --> 19:38.570
they contained mana and could be dangerous.

19:38.570 --> 19:42.440
So I hurried here with my troops.

19:42.700 --> 19:45.080
I see there were undead creatures.

19:45.080 --> 19:47.320
What happened to your barrier?

19:47.320 --> 19:49.820
It wouldn't activate for some reason.

19:50.490 --> 19:52.520
How unfortunate.

19:52.520 --> 19:57.110
No wonder all these adventurers 
struggled to contain them.

19:57.110 --> 20:00.060
I'm glad we made it here in time.

20:01.430 --> 20:05.530
Either way, I'm glad you're
 all right, Lady Sasha.

20:05.530 --> 20:09.260
I certainly hope Lady Helvetica fared as well.

20:09.260 --> 20:12.650
My sister is at the estate,
which should be safer than here.

20:12.650 --> 20:16.100
Oh, she's at the estate, is she?

20:16.100 --> 20:18.540
I see. I do pray she's all right.

20:18.540 --> 20:20.500
How dare he when he showed up late.

20:20.890 --> 20:22.510
Who does this pig think he is?

20:22.890 --> 20:27.150
What? What did you just say, girl?

20:27.150 --> 20:31.290
Only the worst adventurers 
show up late for just the best parts.

20:31.290 --> 20:33.370
In other words, you're trash.

20:33.950 --> 20:36.750
Silence, girl!

20:36.750 --> 20:38.570
Sister! Seren!

20:38.960 --> 20:39.850
What?!

20:40.800 --> 20:44.380
Count Malta. As the countess of Bordeaux,

20:44.380 --> 20:47.180
I thank you for traveling 
so far to bring reinforcements.

20:48.150 --> 20:50.940
Wh-Why, you're welcome.

20:51.260 --> 20:54.480
Milord, even for a man of your station,

20:54.480 --> 20:58.070
it would be inappropriate to remain mounted.

21:01.280 --> 21:04.200
Now that you've brought 
your men all the way here,

21:04.200 --> 21:07.080
you'll help keep watch tonight, won't you?

21:10.330 --> 21:12.160
But of course.

21:12.460 --> 21:16.340
Looks like he didn't expect me to survive.

21:16.340 --> 21:18.670
Even so, we have no evidence against him.

21:18.670 --> 21:20.590
We must move carefully.

21:20.590 --> 21:22.630
Yes, I know.

21:28.140 --> 21:29.000
Ange!

21:30.120 --> 21:32.050
What's wrong? Are you hurt?

21:32.050 --> 21:33.300
Are you all right?

21:33.990 --> 21:35.440
I'm fine.

21:36.740 --> 21:38.940
I see. That's good.

21:38.940 --> 21:42.780
But I feel weak. Carry me.

21:43.600 --> 21:46.360
All right. Hop on.

21:51.020 --> 21:54.200
You're the same... the same...

21:55.350 --> 21:58.710
<i>No. I'm me.</i>

23:35.060 --> 23:40.010
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.060 --> 23:40.010
<b>"A Long Night and a Bright Dawn"</b>
